          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കള്ളൻ — kaḷḷan — \"a thief\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇന്നലെ രാത്രി ഒരു കള്ളൻ ഞങ്ങളുടെ വീട്ടിൽ കയറി. innale rātri oru kaḷḷan ñaṅṅaḷuṭe vīṭṭil kayaṟi. Last night a thief got into our house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: കള്ളന്മാർ, kaḷḷanmār."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman thief is കള്ളി. Also said, half in fun, of a cheeky child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കള്ളൻ (kaḷḷan) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1372 groups Malayalam kaḷḷan, \"thief, liar, rogue\", with Tamil kaḷ, \"to steal\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
